    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is genuinely balanced between the bull and bear cases for JPM. The bull case rests on a fully aligned moving-average stack, a +22% 60-day run, and a fortress balance sheet, while the bear case documents a real momentum divergence (RSI fell 8 points from its Jan 30 peak of 73.27 while price sits just 0.9% below its high), a flatline MACD histogram at +0.01, and declining volume (relative volume at 0.78x the 20-day mean). Critically, there is an information vacuum \u2014 no news, no sentiment, and a balance sheet snapshot five months stale (September 2023) \u2014 which makes a high-conviction directional bet unjustified. The stock has already run +22% in 60 days, so much of the easy upside may be priced in. The responsible stance is to hold the current position while awaiting either a confirmed breakout above $167.25 on strong volume (relative volume > 1.2x) to validate the bull, or a breakdown below the Bollinger middle band at $162.48 on rising volume to validate the bear.\n\n**Entry Price**: 165.79\n\n**Stop Loss**: 162.48\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral/benchmark weight. Do not deploy new capital until a confirmed trigger (breakout above $167.25 on volume > 1.2x, or breakdown below $162.48 on rising volume) is established.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
